{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.DecayFunctionalUnification","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayFunctionalUnification","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.alpha_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.alpha_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFunctionalUnification.lean#L175-L179","doc":"`α = 0` exactly at `z = 1`, so both coordinates are anchored at the same\npoint — which is why leading-order agreement is automatic and carries no\ninformation about which reading is correct. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.alpha_two_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.alpha_two_mul","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFunctionalUnification.lean#L167-L172","doc":"The ladder phase is the counit-minus-trace discrepancy, `2α = ε − tr_M^z`.\nThe corpus's *\"α is neither free nor fitted: it IS the discrepancy\"*, recorded\nhere so both coordinates sit in one file. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.traceFunctional_eq_QA_mul_affine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.traceFunctional_eq_QA_mul_affine","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFunctionalUnification.lean#L149-L165","doc":"The trace functional, with `K = 𝔈₀`, is `Q_A` times the affine correction:\n`𝔈₀·(−tr_M^z(Δ_S))·(2q − q² + 1) = Q_A·(2qz − q² + 1)`.\n\nThis is the unification in one line. The ladder asserts the same left-hand side\nequals `Q_A · cos(α − u/2) · Π_k(1 + c_k u^k)`; equating the two therefore\n*defines* the `c_k` as the ratio of an affine function of `z` to a cosine of an\naffine function of `z`, with no independent content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.traceRatio_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.traceRatio_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFunctionalUnification.lean#L143-L147","doc":"The affine correction is `1` exactly at `z = 1`, matching `traceDelta_one`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.traceRatio_sub_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.traceRatio_sub_one","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFunctionalUnification.lean#L135-L140","doc":"The same statement as a ratio, given a non-vanishing denominator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.traceNum_sub_denom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.traceNum_sub_denom","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFunctionalUnification.lean#L125-L132","doc":"The affine correction departs from `1` linearly in `z − 1` with slope `2q`,\nstated on the numerators so no non-vanishing hypothesis is needed. Non-zero slope\n(`q ≠ 0`) is why the trace inversion for `z` is exact and unique rather than a\nfit — and, since the ladder's cosine has a different slope at `z = 1`, why the\ntwo routes report different `z` for one measured correction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.traceDelta_cross_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.traceDelta_cross_mul","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFunctionalUnification.lean#L115-L122","doc":"**The correction factor is affine in `z`**, in cross-multiplied form so no\nnon-vanishing hypothesis on the counit is needed:\n`tr_M^z(Δ_S)·(2q − q² + 1) = ε(Δ_S)·(2qz − q² + 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.E0_mul_counit_eq_QA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.E0_mul_counit_eq_QA","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFunctionalUnification.lean#L102-L113","doc":"**The bridge.** `𝔈₀ · (−ε(Δ_S)) = Q_A`, identically in `q` and `m_e`.\n\nSo the ladder's leading term is the trace functional at `z = 1` with the scale\n`K = 𝔈₀`. This is `prop:neutron-qvalue-symbolic` stated as an identity: the two\ndecay readings do not merely agree numerically at leading order, they are the\nsame expression. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.traceDelta_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.traceDelta_one","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFunctionalUnification.lean#L97-L100","doc":"The trace evaluated at `z = 1` **is** the counit. The two corpus closed\nforms are one object at the augmentation point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.alphaOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.alphaOf","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFunctionalUnification.lean#L93-L94","doc":"The ladder phase `α = (z−1)h/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QA","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFunctionalUnification.lean#L88-L91","doc":"The ladder's leading term `Q_A = m_e·|q²−2q−1|·(q+1)/(2q³)`, written with the\nsign it carries on the substrate branch (`q² − 2q − 1 < 0` for `q` near `q₀`), so\nthe identity below is an equation and not an equation-up-to-sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.E0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.E0","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFunctionalUnification.lean#L84-L86","doc":"The canonical hadronic energy scale `𝔈₀ = m_e/(q(q−1))` — the corpus's\nderived trace→MeV conversion, fixed by CAL-1 and CAL-2 alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.traceDelta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.traceDelta","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFunctionalUnification.lean#L80-L82","doc":"The Markov trace of the short decay element at Markov parameter `z`,\n`tr_M^z(Δ_S) = h²/2 − h·z`. Corpus closed form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.counitDelta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.counitDelta","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFunctionalUnification.lean#L76-L78","doc":"The counit (augmentation) of the short decay element, `ε(Δ_S) = h²/2 − h`.\nCorpus closed form; `qbeta-counit-closed-form.md`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.hOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.hOf","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFunctionalUnification.lean#L73-L74","doc":"The substrate variable `h = q − 1/q`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}